    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="68.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 68.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.19"/> hwa hwæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.20"/> ungewealdes gedeð, ne byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.17"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eallunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.21"/> na gelic, þe hit gewealdes gewurþe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.star3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf hwa ungewealdes hwæt gedeð, ne byð þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eallumga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.8"/> gelíc ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.9"/>, ðe hit gewealdes deð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="354" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa ungewealdes gedeð, ne bið þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eallum na gelic, þe hit gewealdes gedeð.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quisquam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.14"/> agat aliquid inpossibiliter, non est omnino simile, si uoluntarie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.15"/> faciat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis quicquam imprudenter fecerit, non erit consimile, ac si prudenter factum fuisset.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="68.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf hwa ungewealdes hwæt<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.4"/> gedeð, ne byð þæt eallunga<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.5"/> gelíc ðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.6"/> ðe hit gewealdes deð<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="288" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa hwæt ungewealdes gedeð, ne byð þæt eallunga na gelic þe hit gewealdes gedeð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="355" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn einer etwas unabsichtlich verübt, ist das nicht gänzlich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_68-3.lnote.de.1"/> gleich (dem <hi rend="italic">B</hi>), der es absichtlich verübt (dass es a. geschieht <hi rend="italic">G</hi>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone does something unintentionally, that is not wholly the same as (as the one, B) who does it intentionally (as its happening intentionally, G).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone does anything unintentionally, the case is entirely different from that of one who acts deliberately.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone does anything unintentionally, it is not at all the same as if it happened by intention.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="289" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone does something unintentionally, then it is not to be treated in any way as if the act were carried out with intent.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="355">Can. Edg. Conf. 4</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd.</note>
        <note type="editorial">A and Ld read ‘gedeð’ for G's ‘gewurþe’, which Liebermann thinks more original (the Canons of Edgar have ‘misdeð’). Liebermann compares Canons of Edgar, Confessional 4.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 355, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hwæt: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">na: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gedeð: gewurþe G; deð B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> -lunga <hi rend="italic">oder</hi> -lum na</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read -lunga or -lum na</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Can. Eg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Can. Eg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quis al. agat <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quis al. agat K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rię <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rię Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eallum na gelice <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eallum na gelice Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">354</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Consil.;</hi> gedeð <hi rend="italic">A Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">originaler:</hi> misdeð <hi rend="italic">Can. Eg.</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Consil.; gedeð A Ld [more original: misdeð Can. Eg.]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_68-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">eallum</hi> in A kann Instr. pl. sein, ist aber mit adverbialem Sinne nicht belegt; sg. <hi rend="italic">ealle</hi> und <hi rend="italic">mid eallum</hi> kommt für ‘gänzlich’ vor; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Absicht 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">eallum</hi> in A may be an instr. pl., but is not attested with an adverbial sense; the sg. <hi rend="italic">ealle</hi> and <hi rend="italic">mid eallum</hi> occur for ‘entirely’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Absicht 4</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>hwæt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>eallunga</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">eallumga</hi> B; -<hi rend="italic">unga na</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">eallum na</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>ðam</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_68-3.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>deð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gewurþe</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">gedeð</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
